--syscall-view for ai-jail 3.5.0 (from the fork's feat/syscall-view, merged into
the Zeo stack zeo/ebuild-350-r4): with --mask-host, uname(2) and sysinfo(2)
are answered by ai-jail outside the sandbox through a seccomp user-notify
filter the in-sandbox helper installs before its deny filter, so `uname -r`,
Python's platform and `getconf _PHYS_PAGES` agree with the host view's files:
the numeric release, the sandbox's host name, its age as uptime, no load,
memory sized to the limit. Opt-in, Linux only, never saved; only the native
architecture is trapped. Must follow ai-jail-host-view-extra.patch. Design:
zeo-workspace docs/HOST-VIEW-EXTRA-LAYER.md §4.3.

